Description: Preserve signed 8-bit Datum conversions on PostgreSQL 19
 PostgreSQL 19 removed Int8GetDatum, but upstream still uses it through
 PG_RETURN_INT8 and directly in series/int8.c. Restore the former signed
 conversion only when the macro is absent. CharGetDatum is unsuitable
 because plain char signedness varies by architecture.
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-21

--- a/int_utils.h
+++ b/int_utils.h
@@ -43,6 +43,11 @@
 
 #ifndef PG_GETARG_INT8
 #define PG_GETARG_INT8(n)	 DatumGetInt8(PG_GETARG_DATUM(n))
+#endif
+
+/* PostgreSQL 19 removed this signed 8-bit Datum conversion. */
+#ifndef Int8GetDatum
+#define Int8GetDatum(x) ((Datum) (int8) (x))
 #endif
 
 #ifndef PG_RETURN_INT8
